  "term": "dys-",
  "definition": "Dys- is a prefix used to show that a function or activity is impaired, defective, or difficult. In a more specific historical sense, it points to troubled performance rather than complete absence of ability or an excessive amount of it, and may emphasize difficulty rather than a distorted form of action.",
